            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jennifer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 1 medium-ish head of cabbage, and substituted celery for the peppers ( didn’t have any on hand!). I halved all the other ingredient amounts. THIS right HERE is a recipe that SHOULD be TRIED! It is delicious, the family LOVED it! I served it with grilled kielbasa with a little brown sugar rubbed on it and yesterday’s leftove hash brown potatoes. Big hit. Thanks for the great recipe. I used 1 &amp; 1/2 t. red pepper flakes, it had some heat ( which we loved) but if you don’t like spicy I would cut it down to maybe 1/4 t. Now go make it!!!",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-18T01:05:45.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was looking for a signature relish for my hot dog truck and found this recipe. I followed the recipe to the tee and it turned out awesome. This recipe is supposed to be the recipe used for Slawsa. I had to check and see if they tasted the same. After purchasing some Slawsa and doing the taste test, we decided that this recipe was better than the Slawsa. I will be using this recipe for my slaw dogs on the hot dog truck.m",
            "datePublished": "2018-10-07T16:39:22.217Z"
